-## Protocol configuration contract
-
-Reference mechanisms: Cherry Studio hides dialect settings for system providers; Pi binds native
-API implementations to providers; OpenCode supplies provider-specific SDK loaders; Cindy and
-OpenClaw retain explicit per-route capability metadata. CC Switch presets bind protocol, endpoint
-and model compatibility together. Reuse these boundaries, not their account stores or Agent loops.
-
-The existing Provider template is the only default owner. Unchanged preset endpoint/protocol values
-are inherited rather than copied into a new personal overlay. A pure provider-domain policy is
-shared by setup, the existing editor and host-side config validation. The host rejects a newly
-introduced mismatched protocol at a preset's declared endpoint; editing a custom endpoint or
-creating an untemplated connection keeps all supported adapters available. Declared alternate
-templates are selected atomically before creation, including their model rules. No model-name or
-URL-substring guessing, fabricated support, endpoint rewrite on failure, or subscription-to-API fallthrough.
-
-Existing explicit overrides remain visible and unchanged; unrelated name/key edits must still save.
-Subscription endpoint/protocol/auth kind stay adapter-owned. No storage migration or new authority.
-Event order: local draft → existing config service validates against the current template → one
-repository update → existing Registry/model binding refresh. Discovery starts from committed configuration and rejects
-stale responses. Desktop and remote clients share this host boundary. Neither mounting nor opening
-advanced settings writes configuration. Tests cover host rejection without writes, custom endpoints,
-legacy overrides, subscription isolation, inheritance and actual adapter dispatch.
-
-Plan templates retain regional
-endpoints and explicit API-key authentication: GLM, Kimi Code, MiniMax Token Plan, Alibaba Coding
-Plan / Token Plan, MiMo Token Plan and OpenCode Go. China/global keys are not interchangeable;
-existing saved instances are never rewritten by template updates. Empty catalogs remain manual
-discovery, not fabricated entitlements. All three API formats and same-model key recovery use
-the existing runtime. Adding templates does not certify subscription allowance or live inference.
