-## Official CLI integration decision
-
-Device-code OAuth inside Pi and actual execution by an official CLI are different paths.
-The candidate currently implements the former; it does not execute an official CLI as an Agent.
-Cindy's `claude-native-cli.ts` delegates sign-in and status to the unmodified Claude Code binary,
-then executes it through its SDK. Its former independent Claude OAuth account path is retired.
-Anthropic's current authentication policy allows users to sign into the unmodified CLI and excludes
-third-party token handling; copying Craft's old OAuth form into Pi is not the selected solution.
-Gemini CLI exposes Google AI Pro/Ultra sign-in and ACP. Antigravity's consumer OAuth is restricted;
-its documented enterprise/API SDK is a separate route, not that consumer subscription.
-
-The owner delegated source-backed selection and expanded it to the whole Agent kernel (OV-036).
-The engineering recommendation keeps the current direct-model adapter during comparison and
-evaluates complete native executors, first Claude Code, then Gemini ACP. Fleet would retain one UI Session
-and permission presentation, with each external run attached by identity; no concurrent second
-executor for the same turn, credential scraping or hidden runtime/model switch. Completion requires
-stream, tool permission denial, cancellation, restart/resume, model discovery and native error
-fixtures before the option becomes connectable. Native authentication/multi-account support must
-follow each CLI's documented mechanisms; the current encrypted API/OAuth account pool must not
-pretend to rotate a CLI login. No native executor or kernel migration is implemented by this slice.
-The root Agent-core contract owns promotion criteria; do not add a disconnected login-only entry.
