-## Provider setup and model preferences
-
-The add-provider surface first selects Subscription or API, then a vendor within that category. A plan authenticated with an API key is still a subscription plan; protocol variants are not vendor identities. Custom API creation stays in this page and uses the same provider card, key rows, and format controls. Default conversation selection reuses the existing personal provider repository; preferences must not create another credential or Session owner. Media defaults must be tied to an executable capability, not inferred from image input or a chat model name. CC Switch import reads its database without mutation, previews no raw secrets, imports only selected API connections through the current provider settings owner, and does not change the default model or invoke a billable test.
-
-The extra Default models page and favorite picker group are retired under OV-045. Existing stored preference fields remain compatible leaves of the personal provider envelope; model enablement and the original conversation picker own the active UI. Async preference reads retain their revision; a configuration event invalidates older reads before publication. Saving another favorite must preserve existing unavailable favorites without letting them block unrelated edits; newly added invalid models/effort still fail validation. Provider overlay saves are replacements, so callers preserve untouched provider fields. Preference writes await the existing Registry refresh before a subsequent provider mutation.
