-## Usage costs and subscription payments (OV-047)
-
-Extend the existing model_usage ledger with one accounting_json snapshot per recorded request.
-The existing migration preserves valid raw historical counters without guessing old account,
-speed or price metadata. The request owner records the resolved account and requested speed;
-pricing uses a reported served tier when recognized. Unknown served tiers are not standard by
-default. Cache read/write and reasoning counters remain subsets, never additional total tokens.
-Freeze verified official price version and estimated API value/native credits with the request;
-the supported exact OpenAI and DeepSeek models do not imply other providers have verified prices.
-Automatic thirty-day pruning of lightweight usage facts stops; explicit deletion semantics remain.
-
-The existing usage query provides account/model/speed aggregates and requested date ranges.
-Usage Settings shows per-model cache hit rate, priced/reporting coverage and API-equivalent cost.
-The Token popup retains original capacity/composition/allowance presentation without the rejected
-request-detail disclosure. Actual payments belong to AppSettings.subscriptionPayments, keyed by
-record ID and merged through its serialized writer. Each record binds one saved account (or an
-explicit membership-key connection total), currency and absolute half-open billing period.
-Only providers in Model Settings's added-service scope may supply new payment choices; disabled
-saved plans remain eligible for recording their already-paid bill. Retired built-in offers do not.
-
-Within that period, use native-credit weights only with complete coverage, otherwise complete
-official API-value weights; missing legacy identity/price leaves the amount unallocated. Do not
-sum currencies, guess other-app usage, or claim an unfinished billing period is final. Edits that
-change only the amount preserve original absolute date boundaries after timezone changes.
-Overlap is rejected by both form and settings validation; deleting a payment uses a keyed
-tombstone without modifying the request ledger. Closing an unfinished form writes nothing.
-
-### Original-style statistics and model controls (OV-049)
-
-Use the original AppUsagePanel sequence (summary, heatmap, trend, model chart). The model chart
-owns Token/cache/cost metric tabs; remove the separate accounting table. Reuse its donut, palette,
-legend layout and chart tooltip, with per-model cache bars and unknown/partial coverage in focused
-hints. Keep only the selected metric and actionable state visible, not report-style prose or a
-source-link footer. Pricing source links move to the existing popover pattern. Payment records
-select one account-period, graph its allocation in the same chart pattern, and keep edits in the
-existing form. Currency and exact period remain visible; unavailable allocations never get a pie.
-These are projections of the existing ledger and settings writer, not new accounting state.
-
-The model list uses enable/disable to control availability; remove row deletion controls without
-deleting data or the existing management API. Editing remains the correction path for a mistyped
-manual ID. A native subscription's authenticated catalog owns its models, so hide manual Add there;
-its refresh action reads the account catalog. API connections retain inline manual-ID entry below
-the list, labelled explicitly. Enter confirms only that draft, Escape cancels it, duplicate IDs
-point to the existing list, and failed saves retain input. Adding never invokes paid inference.
-
-### Public price catalog coverage (OV-050)
-
-The existing pure usage-price calculator owns all estimates. A generated, bundled models.dev
-price snapshot expands provider/model coverage; its maintainer sync command validates and replaces
-the snapshot atomically, preserving source URL, retrieval time, hash and MIT notice. No new runtime
-network service, credential store or price database is introduced. Existing officially verified
-OpenAI/DeepSeek schedules take precedence; official Anthropic/Z.AI corrections retain their source.
-Match the recorded provider and exact model ID (unambiguous case normalization is allowed), never
-strip arbitrary suffixes or select the cheapest of several providers. Preserve context thresholds,
-cache categories and missing versus free values; an unpriced field is not zero.
-
-Record the resolved endpoint's catalog provider through the existing accounting metadata. Query
-may derive a current-rate estimate for previously unpriced rows only from recorded facts and known
-builtin provider identities; previously frozen prices remain unchanged. Never fill old account,
-speed or counters from current settings. Catalog availability and incomplete historical usage are
-different failure reasons. Published Z.AI schedules distinguish Flash/FlashX by model ID, so a missing irrelevant speed field does not block their current-rate quote; it remains unknown in usage statistics. The statistics hint identifies current/reference rate coverage without
-adding another visible report or settings page. Existing actual-payment isolation stays unchanged.
-
-### Unified cost analysis and project attribution (OV-051)
-
-One cost-analysis section replaces the unrelated model-estimate tab and subscription-payment card.
-Select either the current global usage range or one saved account/billing period. The same scoped
-request aggregates produce the API-equivalent amount, paid-fee allocation and blended per-million
-input-plus-output token rates. Fee edits update that same projection immediately; API estimates
-remain unchanged. Reuse original summary-strip and comparison-chart primitives. Published prices,
-cache discounts and recorded served speed already enter the existing ledger; do not build another
-pricing store. Show missing coverage in focused help, never invent a cost or account to fill a chart.
-Native credits remain the first allocation basis, then complete API-value weights as approved.
-Compare monetary differences only for USD payments against USD API estimates; do not invent FX.
-
-Capture workspacePath from the existing runtime workspace root in the same accounting_json fact.
-Historical missing project attribution remains a null/unassigned bucket. Compute the complete
-account-period denominator once, then project by model or workspace: the sum of project allocations,
-including unassigned work, must equal the allocated payment. Project panels later consume this same
-projection with their existing folder identity, not a separate ledger or a full monthly bill per
-project. A workspace filter applies after account-period allocation.
-
-The original context ring continues to mean conversation context pressure. Its subscription area
-must distinguish read-only quota inspection, configured default account and last actual execution
-account. Auto recovery must not relabel the default account as the account that served the request.
-Carry the existing local account ID through ModelComplete, V4 lastRequest and retained usage reads;
-never expose tokens. Keep the original popup structure and separate incomparable account windows.
-No inference-account switch or reset redemption happens from the quota-view selector.
-
-Historical usage reads do not require a configured model or active conversation. Reuse the existing
-local control-plane carrier (also used by global workflows) when no reusable local workspace client
-exists. Read the same Session SQLite ledger over v4/usage/stats; do not select an arbitrary remote
-workspace, create a conversation, start inference or add another storage owner.
-
-### CC Switch import correction
-
-Read the external database in one read-only transaction. Translate the source client's actual wire
-URL semantics, not just its displayed base URL: Claude's Chat/Responses proxy adds /v1, while Codex
-adds it only to a bare origin. Strip Claude's local [1M] marker before deduplicating upstream model
-IDs; the marker alone does not prove a context limit. Include explicit catalog and subagent models.
-Import API-key configurations whose declared protocol is supported, including compatible Claude
-Desktop/OpenCode/Pi/OpenClaw shapes; reject OAuth, scripts and unrepresentable per-model routes.
-
-Match existing connections by protocol, credential and canonical/source URL in ProviderSettings,
-not a process-local imported-ID map. Reimport completes the same connection, preserves disabled
-models/manual corrections/defaults and retries missing model writes. Exact known endpoint templates
-supply brand/key-management metadata and plan categorization without inheriting template model lists;
-arbitrary names/hosts do not. Same-key connections across catalog-proven equivalent service routes
-are already bound: retain their current protocol rather than creating or switching a route.
-Selected repair disables erroneous local-marker aliases after their canonical model exists, without
-deleting historical model data. No source changes, inference or default-account/model changes.
-
-Preview → existing ProviderSettings owner → connection/model writes → refreshed settings/picker.
-The preview shows converted protocol/models and whether the selected existing connection is completed.
-A missing upstream model-list endpoint is a localized informational state, not a broken saved key.
-
-
-### Billing and projectless usage correction (OV-052)
-
-Provider-reported billing periods/currency reuse the existing subscription metadata cache and
-account/revision check. A one-period active_start/active_until can prefill the existing fee form;
-long-running subscription start dates cannot stand in for a current billing cycle. Preserve exact
-absolute boundaries unless the user edits dates, and reject late metadata after account or field
-changes. Discounts and list prices never become actual payments without an invoice fact.
-Current live ChatGPT responses expose dates/currency/discounts but no amount paid. No payment is
-automatically fabricated or saved. Amount acquisition remains incomplete for these responses.
-
-Project cost projection uses the existing registered local project list. Conversation backing roots,
-unregistered paths and null history group under Other without rewriting immutable usage facts or
-removing them from account-period allocation. Agent-editable statistics must reuse the existing
-Session/permission and Settings owners; that contextual bridge is not implemented by this change.
-
-### Activity evidence and source-backed charts
-
-Reuse the existing model_usage, turn_usage and tool_usage records and the same usage/stats query.
-The original tool_usage table already owns identity, scope, outcomes, latency, output size, retries
-and permissions. Expose its existing tool aggregate before adding counters. Skill result/error events
-already carry qualified name, plugin ID and source, but those fields are not retained in tool_usage;
-extend that row with nullable metadata, not another event stream or telemetry service. Repeated
-events upsert the same session/tool-call identity. Never infer historical skills from installed lists.
-
-The initial activity view reports tool calls and explicit Skill invocations with outcome/latency.
-Installed/enabled/loaded/executed are distinct; a loaded skill does not prove task success. Actual
-API billing remains per request. Session/turn links permit later associated-cost analysis but do not
-justify billing every tool or skill for a whole model request. Version provenance, accepted outcome,
-before/after configuration cohorts and an Agent read/write bridge still need their own real facts.
-Keep structured facts, not additional copies of prompts, credentials or complete tool output.
-
-Cost presentation follows EvilCharts' grouped horizontal bar pattern over the existing ZCode
-Recharts/ChartContainer. Model/project grouping is separate from total/per-million units. API
-estimates and allocated payments are alternative valuations, not stackable components. Unknowns
-remain gaps; different currencies use separate charts. Reuse original page order, tokens and controls.
-
-
-ReadUsageStats is a read-only tool over the same injected SessionStore usage query, bounded to 7/30
-days. It returns aggregate models/tools/identified skills and price coverage with local-host scope,
-never raw messages, credentials or configuration commands. It remains available independently of
-dynamic workflow gating. Normal tool deny/permission rules apply. It does not claim Agent settings
-editing, automatically disable plugins, change models or allocate per-tool bills. Missing port/data
-returns explicit unavailable/null instead of a fabricated empty account. Human and Agent statistics
-share the same query owner and scope semantics.
-
-### Verified connection status and targeted failure feedback
-
-Registry executable means configuration can be submitted, not that authentication or inference has
-succeeded. Imported/saved connections start unverified. Only an actual completed probe may mark the
-specific tested model successful; failed/late checks cannot leave a green ready signal. UI probe
-observations include the tested model/time and expire when their host, committed configuration revision or settings mount changes. They are not durable account health facts.
-
-Retain the existing model network failure's status/reason/business code through the connectivity
-RPC as a bounded typed result, not a string-only exception. Classify authentication, explicit expired
-subscription/quota, unsupported client, absent model/endpoint, request format/parameters, timeout,
-network and provider failures without guessing expiry from 401/403. Localize summaries and next steps.
-Test failures use the original inline feedback owner; model metadata opens only on explicit edit.
-
-Acceptance: a loopback-only fixture replays the recorded Kimi `access_terminated_error` through the
-built desktop, Host, CLI and actual AI SDK stream path. The Chinese/English message identifies
-missing subscription service access, retains HTTP 403, marks the probe failed and leaves metadata
-closed. A complete synthetic successful stream marks only its tested model successful. Original
-review-profile credentials, default and model parameters are preserved; no paid probe was sent.
-
-### Product identity and subscription tiers
-
-Keep the existing vendor/service/region catalog and credential owner. Within an intake section,
-a vendor group containing one named service uses that product's public service name; multi-service
-groups retain the vendor heading and existing service selector. Generic API groups keep vendor
-identity. Grok subscription uses its own Grok asset and label, while xAI API retains xAI. Membership
-tiers belong to each authenticated account; do not create duplicate login routes per tier or infer
-entitlement from the tier label. Preserve user-authored connection aliases and stable route IDs.
