-Acceptance from an isolated desktop profile: the one saved synthetic key showed no confirm,
-trash, per-key toggle or automatic switch; changing it and blurring saved through ProviderSettings.
-A second unsaved row showed removal but no automatic switch; blurring a distinct second synthetic
-key saved it and enabled the controls. Removing that key collapsed back to the single-row layout.
-Clearing the final key on blur removed its persisted value and disabled discovery. No real key or
-provider request was used. The current Claude subscription lane is still absent, not an API alias.
