-### Effective model facts versus safety defaults
-
-The global `modelMatch: ".*"` rule exists to complete the current runtime contract, but its
-200K context, 32K output, tool support and enabled/disabled effort choices are not provider
-metadata. Keep that runtime fallback until the transport contract can represent unknowns. Add a
-read-only sparse evidence projection from the existing ordered model-rule owner: exact provider
-observations, explicit personal corrections and model-specific built-in recommendations count;
-unqualified wildcard rules do not. Settings must show a value only when that field has evidence,
-and mark built-in recommendations separately from provider-reported data. Unknown remains unknown
-in the model row/editor and must not be advertised as an actual context capacity. The runtime
-fallback remains traceable and is never written into personal corrections by viewing/editing a
-model. No new model store, inferred entitlement or paid test is introduced.
-
-The same evidence projection must reach the selectable model view and the Agent's ListModels
-port. An unknown context must not become a reported 200K capacity in the conversation ring:
-ModelSelected explicitly clears the denominator and ModelComplete omits it; a resume cannot
-resurrect a runtime-only fallback as a measured quota. The runtime may still use its old internal
-completion value for safety until the request budget contract accepts unknowns. An unknown
-reasoning list is omitted from display and Agent choices, while automatic execution remains.
-Changing account/model invalidates the old measured occupancy as before. This projection must
-not change which model, credential or tool executor receives the turn.
-
-For an ordinary API-key OpenAI Chat or Responses route, an output limit sourced only from the
-universal runtime fallback remains an internal turn budget: the request map removes the SDK's
-output-limit field and lets the provider apply its default. A model-specific observed, recommended
-or user-corrected limit/map still goes on the wire. Anthropic Messages requires `max_tokens`, and
-subscription/plan adapters retain their native request contract. This is not a claim that an
-unknown model supports the whole fallback window or output size; provider-specific validation
-and other route budgets remain open.
